# JUCE 8 & C++20 VST3 instrument rules

Full text: **`docs/JUCE8_VST3_PROJECT_RULES.md`**.

## Windows build (when OS is Windows)

- C++20, JUCE 8+, CMake 3.22+
- `cmake -B build -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64`
- `cmake --build build --config Release`
- Rebuild after every DSP/CMake change; fix all MSVC issues before done
- Do not copy to `C:\Program Files\Common Files\VST3\` unless user asks

## Audio thread (all platforms)

- No alloc, locks, or logging in `processBlock`
- `ScopedNoDenormals` first line
- Smooth continuous params with `SmoothedValue` (10–20 ms)
- Prefer `Synthesiser` / `SynthesiserVoice`; `prepare()` all `juce::dsp` in `prepareToPlay`

## Agents

- Terminal / pluginval: Claude Code  
- Inline DSP + Melodee aarch64: Cursor (`linux-vst3-dsp-engineer` lane)

On **Linux cloud**, use `./tools/build-vst.sh` / `build-vst-aarch64-linux.sh` — not MSVC.